! IONEFFECTS with the Gaussian field on one bunch over twelve passes, off for the first two: the ions on a
! current host copy as elegant tracks them, the kicks to the electrons on the device with BEAMBEAM's
! gaussianBeamKick(). Identical here; the
! device's exp and Faddeeva function could differ by rounding
Q1: QUAD, L=0.2, K1=0.9
Q2: QUAD, L=0.2, K1=-0.9
D: DRIF, L=0.4
X: IONEFFECTS
Y: IONEFFECTS
C: CHARGE, TOTAL=1e-9
CELL: LINE=(Q1, D, X, D, Q2, D, Y, D)
BL: LINE=(C, 5*CELL)
